Detach mode for the android live view (supervisor wanted 2 modes: in-UI rail + a detach button). Design: reuse the already-self-contained AndroidLiveView component (talks only to /v1/android/* over fetch, own polling in onMount) — so 'detached' = the same component rendered in another window. No shared state to sync; two live views are already the model (agent + human drive the same device).

KEY ARCHITECTURE FACT: the Tauri window loads http://localhost:8935 directly (tauri.conf.json app.windows[0].url), NOT a tauri:// dist. So the desktop app is a webview pointed at the same HTTP server the browser uses; detach = another window at /android.

Implementation:
- AndroidLiveView: added  {detachable=false, ondetach}. Pop-out button (aria-label'd) in the header, ml-auto, only when detachable. Button lives OUTSIDE the component logic (layout passes ondetach) so the component stays pure and the detached window itself doesn't show the button.
- /android route (frontend/src/routes/android/+page.svelte): renders <AndroidLiveView/> in h-screen. RESURRECTS the standalone page deleted in 7b634ba when the rail replaced it — but now as an OPTION, opened in its own window, not a nav destination.
- +layout.svelte: renamed isSetupRoute -> isChromeless = starts-with /setup OR /android, used in the 3 places (onMount early-return, main {#if} chrome guard, docker-modal guard) so /android renders bare. detachAndroid(): Tauri path (detected via '__TAURI_INTERNALS__' in window — withGlobalTauri is NOT set so __TAURI__ is absent, but __TAURI_INTERNALS__ is always injected) dynamic-imports @tauri-apps/api/webviewWindow, getByLabel('android-live') -> setFocus else new WebviewWindow(label,{url,title,width:420,height:900}); web path window.open(url,label,'popup,...'). url = new URL('/android', location.href).href so it resolves to the right origin/port in both. MOVE semantics: sets androidPanelOpen=false after detaching (chose move over duplicate — cleaner model, avoids 2 screenshot loops hammering the device; noted duplicate is also valid per the collaborative model).
- capabilities/default.json: added core:webview:allow-create-webview-window + core:window:allow-create + core:window:allow-set-focus. Verified exact strings against gen/schemas/windows-schema.json (user is on Windows/WebView2) per CLAUDE.md 'read docs, do not guess Tauri'. The created 'android-live' window has NO capabilities (windows:["main"]) but needs none — AndroidLiveView uses only fetch, no Tauri IPC.
- @tauri-apps/api@^2 added (matches tauri=2 in Cargo.toml). Needed so vite can resolve the dynamic import at build; browser build bundles it in a lazy chunk but never executes it.

Verified: npm run check 0 errors (117 pre-existing a11y warnings elsewhere), npm run build OK (android page emitted, dynamic import resolved, prerender fine), cargo check -p xpressclaw-tauri OK (tauri-build validated the permission strings — would fail on an unknown one).

NOT runtime-tested (couldn't drive the desktop app + emulator here): fahreza should click the pop-out in the installed app to confirm the native WebviewWindow actually opens and the detached view polls. window.open path is standard. Chose JS WebviewWindow API over a Rust command (no Rust change, idiomatic) and over plain window.open-everywhere (unreliable in the Tauri webview).
